{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985918-mages-vampires-changelings-and-the-wyld-west","id":985918,"title":"Mages/Vampires/Changelings and The Wyld West","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T20:36:01-07:00","id":985918,"title":"Mages/Vampires/Changelings and The Wyld West","content":"So, im getting a OWoD campaing set during the Wyld West era. i already got plenty of info from the garous. but im curious to know about the other factions during this time. is there any info or anything you guys could think of that would &quot;Fit&quot; the canon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:38:37-07:00","id":986070,"title":"","content":"Vampires would rather cities, but cangrel in the north forest when enough hunt. Some vampires could be interested about blood by cattle or to fund towns like (Stephen King's) Salem lot.<br /> <br /> The naive North-american faes are the nunnehi. I don't feel inspired to suggest stories.<br /> <br /> Mages? Chorus Celestial vs shamans in the west ex-Mexican zones, and dreamspeakers vs Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T17:21:31-07:00","id":986484,"title":"","content":"I already started a few threads to address those issues already. Started each thread in each of their respective forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/940009-wild-magick-west\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ld-magick-west</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/939997-wild-kindred-west\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/939997-wild-kindred-west\"> Wild Kindred West - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/939997-wild-kindred-west\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/939997-wild-kindred-west </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Or Six shooters, Kindred, and cattle wars? Lol. I am wanting to run a Wild West game (yes that's a WtA supllement) and wanting some insight to Kindred in the </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 10-12-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T20:11:07-07:00","id":986534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985918-mages-vampires-changelings-and-the-wyld-west?p=986070#post986070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages? Chorus Celestial vs shamans in the west ex-Mexican zones, and dreamspeakers vs Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Akashayana migrating with the Chinese immigrants working on the railroads. Or Verbana who settled in various frontier farms along with any number of European immigrants and East coast rural Americans. Or Electrodyne Engineers (precursors to the Sons of Ether who are still part of the Technocratic Union), who do anything from work on engineering projects to acting as local country inventors, solving problems with science(!) in a fundamentally superstitious land.<br /> <br /> I believe the Mage Revised Storyteller's Handbook had a lot to say about the Old West, in its section on alternate settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T23:27:43-07:00","id":986602,"title":"","content":"Have you thought about to use another Weird West setting, like the background of Dead Lands rpg?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:03:01-07:00","id":986737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985918-mages-vampires-changelings-and-the-wyld-west?p=986602#post986602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you thought about to use another Weird West setting, like the background of Dead Lands rpg?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not fit intent, but at some point they did a Wyld West-Deadlands crossover trilogy (novels or comics, I don't remember) which had crossover rules in one of the books. Always meant to pick them up but never got around to it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Found them. It's the &quot;Under a Harrowed Moon&quot; trilogy. They're dime novels. The story had to do with a Garou that ends up in the Deadlands world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 10-13-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:16:39-07:00","id":986800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985918-mages-vampires-changelings-and-the-wyld-west?p=986602#post986602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you thought about to use another Weird West setting, like the background of Dead Lands rpg?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do ST Deadlands, the problem is that my players are way to familiar with the setting by now. so i wanted to try something different, they dont want to see it as a &quot;Reskin&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T11:43:22-07:00","id":986866,"title":"","content":"Why not a uchrony? for example Canada is still controlled by France, West of Northamerica is still Mexican, but masonic lodges managed by French secret agents try to erradicate Catholic Church. Alaska is Russia, or almost, there is a rebellion in all north-west coast. Chinese and Japanese spies go to America to help to start new indigenous rebellion. The coast of gulf of Mexico are attacked by Dutch pirates. Irish slaves are victims of experiments by mad cientifics but somebody can escape from slave colonies. The dessert are the hideout of misterous secrets in the underground caverns. Mines by a lost pre-Colombuan civilitation? German inmigrants arrive to North-east, funding new cities (where almost nobody goes to Christian churchs). A strange character has got the patent rights for a new material: graphene!... and electric motors! A new type of epidemic like rabies, appears, the infected ones who survive becomes more hairy, and worse self-control (not all become psyco-killers but only enough to cause bad reputation).<br /> <br /> Do you remember the teleserie &quot;The adventures of Brico Country&quot; where the main character is played by Bruce Cambell? .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:04:57-07:00","id":986906,"title":"","content":"Crowley, I'd check out 'Frontier Secrets' for the old Wild West Werewolf setting. It has a chapter dedicated to changelings, wraiths, and mages, including not just native mystics but also mad inventors and cold-hearted proto-technocrats of the era. It sounds exactly what you might be interested in. I think there is info about vamps too.<br /> <br /> I also really like the Society of the Weeping Moon, which are featured in the same book. The cult feels a lot like the badguys from the first season of 'True Detective.'<br /> <br /> Tails of the Trails: Mexico also has a lot about vampires also, if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:57:28-07:00","id":986987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985918-mages-vampires-changelings-and-the-wyld-west?p=986866#post986866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not a uchrony? for example Canada is still controlled by France, West of Northamerica is still Mexican, but masonic lodges managed by French secret agents try to erradicate Catholic Church. Alaska is Russia, or almost, there is a rebellion in all north-west coast. Chinese and Japanese spies go to America to help to start new indigenous rebellion. The coast of gulf of Mexico are attacked by Dutch pirates. Irish slaves are victims of experiments by mad cientifics but somebody can escape from slave colonies. The dessert are the hideout of misterous secrets in the underground caverns. Mines by a lost pre-Colombuan civilitation? German inmigrants arrive to North-east, funding new cities (where almost nobody goes to Christian churchs). A strange character has got the patent rights for a new material: graphene!... and electric motors! A new type of epidemic like rabies, appears, the infected ones who survive becomes more hairy, and worse self-control (not all become psyco-killers but only enough to cause bad reputation).<br /> <br /> Do you remember the teleserie &quot;The adventures of Brico Country&quot; where the main character is played by Bruce Cambell? .</div> </div> </div> </div>im doing a sort of Ucrony. the PC's had to timetravel (Thanks mages) to a 1875 where the US now belongs to Pentex (again, Thanks Mages). the timeline is slowly breaking and shattering in the present (The Wyrm is already rising and the world is tearing itself appart). so now the PC's must travel back in time, get help and kill the president of the United Confederacy (a Fomori), while at the same time. The World has sink into new wars vs the Empire of The Worm (USA), with the help of Mages, Imbueds and some Vampires, the PC's must stop this before its too late, before a nuclear weapon explodes during the WWI and forces a Fixed Point in Time (The Point of No Return)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:28:42-07:00","id":987030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/985918-mages-vampires-changelings-and-the-wyld-west?p=986987#post986987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> im doing a sort of Ucrony. the PC's had to timetravel (Thanks mages) to a 1875 where the US now belongs to Pentex (again, Thanks Mages). the timeline is slowly breaking and shattering in the present (The Wyrm is already rising and the world is tearing itself appart). so now the PC's must travel back in time, get help and kill the president of the United Confederacy (a Fomori), while at the same time. The World has sink into new wars vs the Empire of The Worm (USA), with the help of Mages, Imbueds and some Vampires, the PC's must stop this before its too late, before a nuclear weapon explodes during the WWI and forces a Fixed Point in Time (The Point of No Return)</div> </div> </div> </div>I had PC Mages do the &quot;time travel to the Wild West&quot; thing as well. I was lucky enough that it was a setting based game, specifically St. Louis, so I didn't have to make up the rest of the world (except by implication). The PCs were getting over a soiree in the near future (which ten years away, in 2017!) with a foray to the further future and overshot the present on their way home. We had just lost a PC to an Epic Destiny (which unfortunately didn't include hanging out with the rest of them), so the player generated Wild West mage character to join up. Because of that, I had to hammer out the whole &quot;This is what the Traditions are like&quot; document, with some codicils about what was going on with the Technocratic Union as well. Well, actually the Union and the remnants of the Order of Reason. Part of the concept was the ongoing conversion from the Order to the Union and the strange bedfellows it was producing. Order of Reason mages who didn't want to convert to the &quot;new orthodoxy&quot;. The Traditions had their own internal disconnect between the European groups and the non-Europeans and between the mystical haves and have-nots based on the relevant prevalence and position of the various ideologies involved. (The PC ended up being a Doc Holliday-type/snake oil salesmen with working snake out, with both Cosian and Verbena leanings). <br /> <br /> It worked out REALLY well. We spend a good long chunk of the game back in the 1870s. It was great because I could show the genesis of issues they had been dealing with regularly since the game had started. I definitely put all the games into play in an adjunct fashion. The group had interacted with wraiths in modern St. Louis and I had the opportunity for them to meet some of them when they were still alive. I went light on the changelings. They had played a huge role in the wrap-up of the escape from dystopia (yup, that's the dystopia of 2017, so take that for what it's worth). Since I had all my Werewolf Wild West books, I replaced them with some significant werewolf interactions. They had minimial dealings with the vamps back in 2007 and they didn't meddle much in vampire business back in the 19th Century (though I did have it ready in case they decided to go play in that part of the sandbox). Again, it was not to hard as I had set up the &quot;current&quot; St. Louis vampires with a conflicted history, so I just rolled it back. The Prince that had been defeated was the head honcho still, etc. <br /> <br /> Oh and a LOT of historical research. A LOT. Since it was on one location, it wasn't too bad. There was some really intricate and tricky stuff that ended up in a 10 page write up of a cursed family and their haunted homes and breweries and how that all tied in with the family curse and history of one of the PCs. <br /> <br /> It was, overall, a ton of fun. I loved it so much I often contemplate just running a game in that sub-chronicle setting. Or just porting over the basic structure of that version of the World of Darkness Wild/Wyld/Savage West and using it for a game set somewhere else. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}